--- A standard module written in Crow has locals of its own: one named
--- like a function of the program's is still the module's local, indexed
--- where the module writes `name[0]` (core's `read` has `data`, and the
--- protocol's `read_answer` has `lines`). A program names its functions
--- as it likes, in both modes.
fn data[n]
    return n * 2

fn lines[n]
    return n + 1

log[data[21]]
log[lines[1]]
kept = write['/tmp/crow_parity_162_note.txt', 'hello\n']
log[kept.ok]
log[read['/tmp/crow_parity_162_note.txt']]
